This extension adds STAR WARS Battlefront II modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Frosty Mod Manager automatically installed.[/summary]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]EA[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[size=3][b][color=#ea9999]This game does not support symlinks. You must have the mod staging folder and the game on the same drive to use this extension.[/color][/b][/size]

[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Frosty Mod Manager installs to the game folder, recognised by a "frostymodmanager.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Frosty mods with a ".fbmod" file install to the "FrostyModManager\Mods\StarWarsBattlefrontII" folder.[/*]
[*]Plugin (FMM) mods with a ".dll" file install to the "FrostyModManager\Plugins" folder.[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above installs to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Variant selection popup for .fbmod installs[/*]
[*]Includes buttons to download DatapathFix (required for Steam/Epic) and to delete the ModData folder[/*]
[*]Epic (license only, launches in EA App)[/*]
[*]Automatically installs [url=https://github.com/CadeEvs/FrostyToolsuite]Frosty Mod Manager[/url] to a new "FrostyModManager" folder.[/*]
[*]The [url=https://github.com/Dyvinia/DatapathFixPlugin]DatapathFix plugin[/url] can be downloaded using the button in the folder icon on the Mods toolbar. [b][color=#ffff00]DatapathFix is required for mods to work with Steam/Epic.[/color][/b][/*]
[*]Installs .fbmod files to the correct folder for Frosty to see them: "FrostyModManager&#92;Mods&#92;StarWarsBattlefrontII". [b][color=#00ff00]You must launch FMM and finish mod installation using the notification button shown on each deployment.[/color][/b][/*]
[*]All other mods are installed to game root with a fallback notification.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for STAR WARS Battlefront II mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Frosty Mod Manager (tool):

This installer handles Frosty Mod Manager, not mods for it. It exists so users can install Frosty Mod Manager through Vortex, and mod authors normally never package this.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a file named "frostymodmanager.exe" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - If you bundle Frosty Mod Manager inside your mod archive, Vortex treats the whole download as Frosty Mod Manager rather than as your mod. Ship the mod alone and list Frosty Mod Manager as a requirement.

========================================================================

Frosty Mods:

Frostbite mods in Frosty Mod Manager format. Vortex stages them for Frosty rather than deploying them into the game directly.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file with the ".fbmod" or ".fbpack" extensions.

  Installs to: "FrostyModManager\Mods\StarWarsBattlefrontII"

  Common mistakes:
    - These mods still have to be applied through Frosty Mod Manager - installing in Vortex alone does not patch the game.

========================================================================

Plugin (FMM):

Recognised when the archive contains a ".dll" file.

  Installs to: "FrostyModManager\Plugins"

========================================================================

Fallback Installer:

The catch-all. Any archive that matched none of the installers above lands here and is copied across unchanged.

[b][color=#ffff00]NOTE: Landing in the fallback installer is a signal your archive layout needs fixing.[/color][/b]

  Requirements:
    - Reaching this installer usually means the archive was not laid out in a way Vortex recognised.
    - Vortex shows the user a notification when a mod installs through the fallback.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - If your mod lands here unintentionally, re-check the layouts above - users will see a fallback warning and may report the mod as broken.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]
